messages:
alex: Quick FYI — planning a Terraform change to adjust Karpenter provisioner taints + HPA burst settings. Want a quick safety check before I open the PR. Will also move the autoscaler webhook secret path.

maria: Which clusters are impacted and what's the taint key/effect?

alex: All prod and staging provisioners for eu-west-1/us-west-2. Taint I'm adding: karpenter.sh/prefer-evict=true with effect PreferNoSchedule. HPA burst target goes from 200% -> 350% for a short window. Secret path moves from /secrets/autoscaler/webhook to /redwood/autoscaler/webhook-cert.

jamal: Can you paste the Terraform snippet so we can eyeball the exact change? Also worried about immediate scale pressure if many pods burst at once.

alex: Sure — here's the rough TF diff I'm planning to apply:

```hcl
resource "aws_ssm_parameter" "karpenter_taint" {
  name  = "/redwood/karpenter/taint_key"
  type  = "String"
  value = "karpenter.sh/prefer-evict"
}

module "karpenter_provisioner" {
  source = "./modules/karpenter/provisioner"
  name   = var.cluster_name

  taints = [
    { key = aws_ssm_parameter.karpenter_taint.value, value = "true", effect = "PreferNoSchedule" }
  ]
}

resource "kubernetes_horizontal_pod_autoscaler_v2" "api" {
  metadata { name = "api" namespace = "default" }
  spec {
    scale_target_ref { kind = "Deployment" name = "api" }
    behavior {
      scale_up { policy { type = "Percent" value = 350 } }
      stabilization_window_seconds = 60
    }
  }
}
```

maria: That TF looks fine syntactically. Two asks: 1) make sure the karpenter IAM role (service account) has permission to read the SSM/Secrets path; 2) don't change HPA scale up policy cluster-wide — limit to specific namespaces/deployments first.

liz: @alex I can handle the secret rotation/SSM mapping. The webhook expects a TLS secret at client cert path — I'll update the secret manager policy. Note: the Karpenter service account needs kms:Decrypt for the certificate if stored encrypted.

jamal: +1 on namespace-scoped rollout. Also we should coordinate with CA/cluster-autoscaler fallback weighting. If provisioner taints cause more evictions we might see more inter-zone launches. Consider adding a small buffer to reserved nodes in CA config.

alex: Good call. I'll add a fallback weight bump: set provisioner_weight to 1.2 for fallback pools in terraform so CA doesn't kill cheaper spot pools first.

